<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογ-έω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			11.636
		</span></i>, al. (part.); 
			Lacon.
		
		1pl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογίομες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					1002
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογέεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					1.312
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.442
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.492
				</span></i>
			, al.: 
				Ep.
			
			pf.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεμογηώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					830
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Al.</u>
				529
			</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγος</span>):—poet. Verb,
				<i>toil, suffer</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> usu. with a cogn. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσσα γε . . θεῶν ἰότητι μόγησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.214
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλα πόλλ᾽ ἔπαθον καὶ πολλ᾽ ἐμόγησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.492
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ μογήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.690
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ ἔπ᾽ ἄλγεα πολλὰ
				μογήσῃ</span> for whom he <i>suffers</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.19
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.162
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα . . ἐμόγησεν ἀμφ᾽ ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.152
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵνεκ᾽ ἐμεῖο πολέας ἐμόγησεν
				ἀέθλους</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				170
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				997
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				71
			</span></i>: abs. in part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ
				ἔργων μογέοντες</span>
			<i>tired</i> after work, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.388
			</span></i>: hence nearly 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγις</span>
			, <i>with pain</i> or <i>trouble, hardly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογέων ἀποκινήσασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.636
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέσαν μογέοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Trag.,
				<i>suffer pain, be distressed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμπονήσατε τῷ νῦν μογοῦντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					277
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ παίσας μογῇς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1624
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μογοῦντα πλευρά</span>
			<i>in</i> the side, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				849
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστοκίαις μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					242
				</span></i>
			 (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοκέες</span> codd.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					830
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκοῖο πάλαι μεμογηότος
				ἄνθην</span> having <i>lost</i> its sheen, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Al.</u>
				529
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>labour at</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λιθουργὸς . . ἐμόγησε κόρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Posidipp.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Tz.
				<u>H.</u>
				7.662
			</span></i>.</div>
